WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:01.930
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:10.590
The year is 1096, it will be 203 years until
the Ottoman empire will begin and start decorating

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:14.139
many a living room with comfortable foot stools.

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:21.730
In 334 years the Aztec empire will be founded
and begin sacrificing 20,000 humans a year,

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:23.690
to keep themselves occupied.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:29.500
And it will be 487 years until the British
Empire start taking over the World by sticking

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.950
flags in things and people.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:39.170
Yet in this year of 1096, what is today the
oldest university in the English-speaking

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:45.980
world, Oxford university, will teach its very
first lesson.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:50.000
One hundred and thirteen years later Cambridge
university will be founded.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.770
Between them both these two powerhouses of
education, spanning back almost a millennium,

00:00:55.770 --> 00:01:02.640
have changed the world in more ways than one
can count and definitely for the better.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:08.080
These two research and education establishments
are responsible for world-altering inventions

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:14.580
and discoveries such as the Theory of Evolution,
IVF, artificial intelligence, heart and lung

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:21.390
transplants, stem cell research, gravity,
the discovery of electrons and nuclear fission,

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:24.630
and last but not least, the internet.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:26.980
And those are just a small selection.

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:33.350
So to try and argue that a University education
is a waste of time and money would be futile,

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:35.310
wouldn’t it?

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:41.340
Well all over the world education has changed
dramatically since the days when the inventor

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:45.720
of the World Wide Web Tim Berners Lee studied
at Oxford University.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:51.670
And it has even changed over the past 15 years,
since Mark Zuckerberg learnt how to ruin the

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:56.770
World Wide Web with Facebook at Harvard University.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:02:03.360
University or college education as our transatlantic
cousins call it, is today less relevant than

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:10.210
ever before in history and for many young
people, attending university could be one

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:15.070
of the most expensive and biggest mistakes
they ever make.

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:19.040
Aside from pre-purchasing No Man’s Sky.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:23.940
All over the developed world we have it drilled
into our heads during our school days that

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:27.459
higher education is the path to gold and riches.

00:02:27.459 --> 00:02:33.760
Get a college diploma they said, get a university
degree they insisted, and you too will be

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:38.700
able to afford champagne, hot tubs and unlimited
naked women.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:44.950
We get told that so frequently by our elders
because when they attended university that

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:47.410
was mostly true.

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:52.120
Thirty years ago if you were lucky enough
to study at university you were pretty much

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:55.849
guaranteed a job in your field of study.

00:02:55.849 --> 00:03:00.890
Engineering graduates would go on to work
for car and aircraft manufacturers, media

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:05.060
students could get a job at a broadcasting
house and so on.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:12.750
Provided you got a decent grade your future
in a well-paid job was almost guaranteed.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:20.620
Today things have changed, on average, only
half of university and college graduates get

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:26.110
a job in the years following graduation and
I’m not even talking about a job that has

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:28.819
anything to do with what they studied.

00:03:28.819 --> 00:03:33.980
Statistics show that many of those 50% of
employed graduates are working in completely

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:42.050
unrelated or menial jobs, because today less
than 30% of all university graduates go on

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:44.990
to work in the field of their degree.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:49.440
Unless you took the The Underwater Basket
Weaving Degree, the demand for them things

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.550
is off the charts.

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:54.349
Yes that is a genuine course.

00:03:54.349 --> 00:03:56.890
The reason behind this has a lot to do with
numbers.

00:03:56.890 --> 00:04:02.069
In the 50s, 60s and 70s only the middle class
and affluent families could afford to send

00:04:02.069 --> 00:04:04.760
their little cretins to university.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:09.870
Even in the UK where university tuition fees
have only existed since 1998, it didn’t

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:15.260
matter because to support the family, children
would have to go off to work at the age of

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:20.439
18 or younger, higher education was just never
an option.

00:04:20.439 --> 00:04:29.800
As a result, in 1950 a pitiful 3% of people
in the UK attended university.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:33.289
Today that has risen to 49%.

00:04:33.289 --> 00:04:40.729
That’s obviously a really good thing, as
a society we are all now more driven and more

00:04:40.729 --> 00:04:48.639
financially able to attend university and
educate ourselves in any field we choose.

00:04:48.639 --> 00:04:53.979
But the problem is, the number of jobs available
has hardly risen at all.

00:04:53.979 --> 00:05:00.180
With so many hundreds of thousands of graduates
each year in the UK and over 4.5 million new

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:07.069
graduates each year in the US, the competition
for the specialised, high paying jobs is greater

00:05:07.069 --> 00:05:08.839
than ever before.

00:05:08.839 --> 00:05:14.339
And if you graduated in something more general
that isn’t so specialised, such as media

00:05:14.339 --> 00:05:20.409
or business studies, then good luck to you,
because you’ve a got an extremely tough

00:05:20.409 --> 00:05:22.610
journey ahead of you.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:27.960
If you currently are or have been in this
situation yourself you will know how horrible

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:34.889
it feels, but if not, imagine spending two
to five years at university studying hard,

00:05:34.889 --> 00:05:40.779
sitting through countless lectures with a
hangover and living off nothing but the two

00:05:40.779 --> 00:05:46.289
important student food groups, instant noodles
and whatever you just found in the cupboard

00:05:46.289 --> 00:05:47.550
on toast.

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:53.330
But finally, after the seemingly longest and
hardest years of your life so far, you have

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:58.749
a moment of glory, you graduate, you throw
your cap into the air and you are filled with

00:05:58.749 --> 00:06:02.960
optimism for the fruitful career that awaits
you.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:07.280
Then six months later you’re working in
a call centre, still eating your typical student

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:08.710
diet.

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:16.159
Now imagine all that but you are also joyfully
over £50,000 in debt.

00:06:16.159 --> 00:06:22.129
And this exact situation is not just befallen
on a fringe group of graduates, the majority

00:06:22.129 --> 00:06:29.509
of university graduates, over 70% find themselves
in a career they never wanted, and almost

00:06:29.509 --> 00:06:34.210
100% will be in debt for the next 30+ years.

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:40.479
I’m not here to say whether Universities
should be free or not, because truthfully,

00:06:40.479 --> 00:06:44.180
there are incredibly strong arguments on both
sides of that fence.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:48.949
On one hand, charging tuition fees makes students
value and appreciate the opportunity more

00:06:48.949 --> 00:06:51.210
strongly and they tend to put more effort
in.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:56.951
Also, without having to rely on government
handouts universities can also offer a higher

00:06:56.951 --> 00:07:01.389
quality of education and more resources for
students.

00:07:01.389 --> 00:07:07.020
But conversely, if university fees are completely
abolished, a greater diversity of people are

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:12.199
given an opportunity to better themselves
and in the long-term it actually pays off

00:07:12.199 --> 00:07:18.310
for the government and society, because a
generally better educated society are going

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:23.619
to contribute more to the country’s economy
in the future through increased innovation

00:07:23.619 --> 00:07:24.619
and business.

00:07:24.619 --> 00:07:29.310
The Shittin’ Shake Weight didn’t invent
itself you know!

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:35.349
University or college graduates are also statistically
far less likely to be involved in crime, reducing

00:07:35.349 --> 00:07:42.400
policing and prison costs and are less likely
to rely on social welfare during their lifetime.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:46.300
Just think about it, when was the last time
you saw a Doctor of Theoretical Physics having

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:50.449
a custody battle with their sister on Jeremy
Kyle?

00:07:50.449 --> 00:07:56.069
Each year millions of young people graduate
from university but a poll recently conducted

00:07:56.069 --> 00:08:03.460
in the UK showed that one-third of university
graduates regret going to University in the

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:04.460
first place.

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.560
So what’s the issue here?

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:11.149
Do students just regret how much money they
spent on instant noodles and booze?

00:08:11.149 --> 00:08:14.279
Probably, but that’s not the main issue.

00:08:14.279 --> 00:08:18.360
Whether you paid for your tuition or not,
the problem is what you’re actually getting

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:23.339
in return for your hard spent time and money.

00:08:23.339 --> 00:08:29.719
When polled 49% of graduates said they could
have gotten the job they are currently doing

00:08:29.719 --> 00:08:34.510
without ever attending University.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:38.610
The problem isn’t just the sheer number
of university graduates out there and the

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:40.780
huge competition.

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:47.550
Over the years the true value of a university
degree has been eroded away to become increasingly

00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:50.960
worthless, just like Windows.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:56.560
Over recent years the percentage of university
graduates achieving a first or 1:1 has risen

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:58.200
sharply.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:03.510
In the UK ministers have spoken out about
how they believe Universities are increasingly

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:09.210
making it easier in sneaky ways, for their
students to achieve higher marks so that the

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:16.020
establishment looks better on paper and they
can better compete in University league tables.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:21.090
And to make things worse, it’s believed
that in many universities across the globe

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:28.050
corruption and abuse of funds is rife, if
the reports are to be believed then it’s

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:31.230
particularly bad in US higher education.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:37.430
Surely the 50 thousand plus you borrowed to
attend university is put to good use?

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:43.080
It’s spent on hiring the best teachers and
purchasing the best facilities for students,

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:44.340
is it not?

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:50.560
Well yes, a lot of it is, but many journalists
have uncovered a seedy underbelly in many

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:52.560
top universities.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:10:07.360
Many higher up staff, such as University presidents
earn more than many CEOs of big corporations.

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:13.750
Apart from day to day management, the primary
role of a University president is fundraising.

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:20.010
This involves horrendously arduous tasks,
such as wining and dining international visitors,

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:24.750
or even jet setting off to exotic locations
for days at a time for “meetings”.

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:34.190
And of course, University funds are used to
pay for all of these activities.

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:39.350
Universities have long been viewed as non-profit
establishments, but journalists believe that

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:46.370
today many large American universities are
acting more like for-profit corporations.

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:53.130
They are increasingly engaging in patenting
and licensing of ideas, concepts and innovations,

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:58.590
which only opens up opportunities to profit
from an idea and is directly contradictory

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:01.070
to providing open education for all.

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:07.040
And this is just scratching the surface, Unesco
released a report called “Corrupt schools,

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:09.840
corrupt universities: What can be done?”

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:14.120
after six years of investigation into schools
and universities worldwide.

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:20.290
The report claims that education at all levels
is corrupted with embezzlement, illegal registration

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:24.740
fees and academic fraud, among other shady
practices.

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:30.900
I’m not trying to put anyone off higher
education, for so many people it can absolutely

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:35.740
be the right choice and the best thing they
will ever do.

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:41.120
But if you are turning against the idea, then
what are your alternatives?

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:46.170
Well, unfortunately if your dream is to be
a doctor, dentist or engineer I’m afraid

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:51.270
you will have to attend university, since
they are strictly regulated, after all, would

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:56.850
you want to operated on by a surgeon who got
their diploma from the university of YouTube?

00:11:56.850 --> 00:12:02.211
But those specific careers aside, the only
thing stopping you from achieving your dream

00:12:02.211 --> 00:12:05.050
job is your passion.

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:11.930
The most important thing you can do in your
professional life is whatever makes you happy,

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:17.240
if you’re about to start your career, you
may think that by opting for a well-paid but

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:24.251
boring job you will have a happy life, but
I promise you the day will come when you will

00:12:24.251 --> 00:12:26.180
wish you followed your true passion.

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:31.190
And if you’re already 30 years down the
line and you already realised this 20 years

00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:36.140
ago, then I’m truly sorry my friend, I think
it’s about time for your mid-life crisis,

00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:40.060
if you like I can just give you a list of
numbers for Porsche dealerships.

00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:47.240
But today, with the internet, the opportunities
to do what you love are limitless, and literally

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:53.780
the only thing stopping you from doing what
you love, is your willingness to try and if

00:12:53.780 --> 00:12:57.180
you stick around until the end of this video,
I’ll tell you a story that will make you

00:12:57.180 --> 00:13:03.190
want to stop everything you’re doing and
follow your dreams, no matter how big they

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:04.190
are.

